1
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:11,140
Turn on the lights and try stepping away from the room,
will you?

2
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,800
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

3
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:47,180
Fuhahahaha!

4
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

5
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

6
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:12,000
Look, even Akaneru is burning up.

7
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:18,260
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

8
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

9
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,380
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

10
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:42,900
A man lives for ambition.

11
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,560
What's with this mountain of curry?

12
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:55,220
Are you opening a curry shop or something?

13
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,080
No.

14
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:58,680
I just bought this curry cheap,

15
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,200
flipped it straight for a profit,

16
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,700
just trying to make some middleman margin.

17
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,100
Middleman margin?

18
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,620
But when the time finally came,

19
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:09,240
the retail store I was supposed to sell to backed out on me,
damn it.

20
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:14,780
Hey, this curry only has two
weeks left until its best-by date.

21
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,820
That's why it was cheap, isn't it?

22
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:19,000
Of course they turned it down.

23
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,440
Damn it, all that's left is debt!

24
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,300
The curry's left too, isn't it?

25
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:26,300
Shut up,
I know that without you having to tell me.

26
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,620
So what exactly do you plan to do?

27
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:31,040
Nakagawa, buy it from me, please!

28
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:34,380
I can't just say something
like that out of the blue.

29
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:38,160
You're rich,
so surely a little bit wouldn't hurt?

30
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:41,000
It's not a little!
How many are there, anyway?

31
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,820
There are a hundred cardboard boxes,
each with a hundred servings.

32
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,200
So that's ten thousand servings?

33
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:50,460
Terai, how about your place?
One box for your family of four?

34
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:54,200
We have kids, so we only eat mild curry.

35
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,200
What about you, Reiko?

36
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:59,040
I've decided that I only eat curry
when I go to Thailand or India.

37
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,860
That's it!
If it comes to this, I'll eat it all myself!

38
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:11,085
It's pitiful, but if we keep going
along with Ryo-chan's nonsense,

39
00:03:11,135 --> 00:03:12,720
it'd cost more than the national budget.

40
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,240
It can't be helped, I suppose.

41
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:14,720
Yeah.

42
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:18,420
Oh no! There's no rice, so I can't cook any!

43
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:20,480
Well, then.

44
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:24,880
If it comes to this, I'll eat nothing but curry,
eating and eating and eating!

45
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:30,020
Curry alone really has its limits.

46
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:31,380
I want rice.

47
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:33,540
My lord.

48
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:36,180
Honda, you showed up at just the right time!

49
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:37,180
Want some curry?

50
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,400
No curry, no curry.

51
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:41,320
I don't have time for that today.

52
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,740
Actually, I want to buy a car.

53
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:47,860
So, senpai,
I was hoping you could come along with me.

54
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:51,240
You, buying a car or
motorcycle or something?

55
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:53,060
Well, that's the thing, senpai...

56
00:03:54,880 --> 00:04:01,280
We always end up taking two bikes, so maybe it'd be nice
to go for a drive together sometimes, just the two of us.

57
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:04,100
Just kidding! Heh. Ahahaha!

58
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:08,400
I'm good at haggling, right, senpai? If
I can get it cheap, I'll thank you for it.

59
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:11,022
A thank-you? Or a middleman's cut?

60
00:04:11,072 --> 00:04:14,060
Right now I want to make up for the curry losses,
even a little.

61
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:17,480
Alright, leave it to me. Really, senpai?

62
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,320
In that case, hurry up! Let's go!

63
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:20,960
Yahoo!

64
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,720
Senpai, where are you going?

65
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,820
Patrol.

66
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:28,420
That's not true. What about the
mountain of curry in the back?

67
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:32,000
I haven't forgotten, so it's fine.
I'll deal with it later. See ya.

68
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:36,280
You're definitely going
to forget about the curry.

69
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,680
So what kind of car do you want?

70
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,040
It'd be the best if I could
drive a Porsche or something.

71
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,800
A Porsche Alright. So what's your budget?

72
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,660
I've got 100,000 yen.

73
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:49,360
100,000?
That's a bit short even for a down payment.

74
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,700
That's all of it.
I'm counting on you for the lease call.

75
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,400
A 35-year loan?

76
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:04,360
It's not a housing loan, so a term that
long isn't really something we can do.

77
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:09,160
The price is practically the cost of a house!
Do something about it.

78
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:14,660
Even so, a luxury car has value
that matches its high price.

79
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:20,640
Senpai, the Porsche was just a joke. No matter how you look at it,
100,000 yen won't work.

80
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:23,160
You get timid the moment
you step off the bike.

81
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:27,880
Well then, don't you have something cheap?
Like a family Porsche?

82
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,100
Understood, we have something like that.

83
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:34,580
We'll prepare a Porsche
that's just right for you.

84
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:38,000
See? It pays to ask, doesn't it, Honda?

85
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,100
Yeah, but is that really true?

86
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:42,260
This way, please.

87
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,620
Whoa, it's small.

88
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:47,740
The copper Porsche-shaped
ashtray is 20,000 yen.

89
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:50,680
Hey, how are you supposed
to ride this thing?

90
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:53,500
We want the real thing. The real thing!

91
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:58,620
However, as a rule, our store
doesn't offer very long-term loans.

92
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:01,900
Without a loan, how are we supposed
to buy such an expensive car?

93
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:07,400
Well, well, welcome, Mr. Miyashita!

94
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,880
Hey, I'm not done with
my business over here yet!

95
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:10,380
This one...

96
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,480
this is the new model that
just came in last week.

97
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:17,720
Not bad at all. How much is it?

98
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:22,760
Including the fees and miscellaneous charges,
it comes to about 35 million yen.

99
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,800
35 million?

100
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,140
That's expensive.

101
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:28,460
35 million

102
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:31,040
Then I'll take one.

103
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:38,720
Thank you very much. I'll start the paperwork right away,
so please come this way.

104
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:42,460
Every time I come to this shop, I end up impulse buying.
It's such a problem.

105
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:48,680
Yeah, a new car's out of the question I know someone who deals in used cars,
so I'll go there instead. Yes.

106
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,660
Hey, Ryo-san!

107
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:59,880
Boss, my budget is just 100,000 yen.
I want a cheap Porsche. Do you have one?

108
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:04,040
Mr. Ryotsu, even a used car lot
can't sell a Porsche for 100,000 yen.

109
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:07,060
A Porsche? We've got one for 80,000 yen.

110
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,420
It's brand-new and shiny, right?

111
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,880
Wow, this one's only 80,000 yen

112
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:20,420
How about it? Even if you pay me a 20,000 yen middleman fee,
you're still within budget, right?

113
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:24,200
Yeah, but does this thing actually run?

114
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:30,180
See? It runs just fine, doesn't it?

115
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,920
Getting this for 80,000 yen is like a dream.

116
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,760
Looks like Yakko-san really likes it.

117
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:37,960
Glad to hear it.

118
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:39,820
Wow, that's so cool.

119
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:44,680
I'll invite Nana right away and go for a drive all the way to Chiba,
vroom vroom vroom.

120
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:48,320
Only, since it's a kit car,
we can't get license plates for it.

121
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:51,660
I had a feeling there was a catch.

122
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:54,820
If you can't get plates,
you can't drive it on the road, can you?

123
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:58,400
Driving it around your own backyard,
or displaying it in the alcove to admire.

124
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,300
There are plenty of ways to use it,
you know.

125
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,940
No way, I want to drive it outside!

126
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,160
What a selfish guy.

127
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:06,500
Well then,
let's take a look at the other cars.

128
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:12,860
At 30,000 yen, then

129
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:15,260
It doesn't look great,
but it can run outside.

130
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,060
That's quite an old model.

131
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:18,660
Does it actually run properly?

132
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:21,380
Of course it still runs fine.

133
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:23,260
It's pretty rusted over.

134
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:26,120
That rust gives it real character.

135
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:29,280
Some people even make rust
on purpose with salt water.

136
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:31,200
Natural rust is the best.

137
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,300
The tires are bald.

138
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,640
What are you talking about, Ryo-san?

139
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:37,120
Racing cars don't have tread, you know.

140
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,260
They've been sanded
down and polished smooth.

141
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:44,400
Well, even if you pay my 70,000 yen commission,
you won't have the budget, will you?

142
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,400
The Porsche won't budge a single yen,
so it's even tougher.

143
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:51,700
It's also unacceptable that the
commission costs more than the car.

144
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,320
You greedy guy.

145
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,400
Which one is greedy?

146
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:56,580
How about this one?

147
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:58,520
It's clean and has plenty of horsepower.

148
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,720
50,000 yen is fine.

149
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:02,900
30,000 yen down,
and installments are fine too.

150
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:10,280
No way. We're not going out for a drive,
so I want a more stylish, cool car

151
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:15,840
to ride in. What are you talking about? Depending on how you look at it,
this is a stylish, cool convertible

152
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:23,180
if you say that, I won't pay the commission.
That's not what we agreed on, is it?

153
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:26,380
Because it keeps getting further
and further from what I want.

154
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:32,000
Your plan to get a stylish, cool car on a
100,000 yen budget was naive from the start.

155
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,880
Didn't you say you were a haggling pro, senpai?
That's why I had high hopes.

156
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:39,860
Found it! A cheap, clean left-hand-drive one

157
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:46,180
It's a Rolls-Royce, isn't it?

158
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:48,240
And it's only 20,000 yen?

159
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,640
You won't find a better deal than this.

160
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:55,260
But there must be a reason
it's only 20,000 yen.

161
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:59,780
Wait, boss, what's going on?
What are you hiding now?

162
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:01,720
Just come out and tell us.

163
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:05,400
W-well, actually,
this car was in an accident.

164
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:09,520
There's a rumor that every
owner is sure to be cursed.

165
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:12,520
It went around and around,
and we took it in cheap.

166
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:16,100
Maybe because the price is too low,
people are wary, and no one will buy it.

167
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:19,220
We couldn't get rid of it,
so it's been sitting there ever since.

168
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,000
A curse.

169
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,180
Is that all? Just that?

170
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,320
"Just that"? It's a curse, senpai!

171
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:28,260
That's just superstition.

172
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:33,460
Now with car navigation, airbags,
and a curse as standard equipment!

173
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:34,140
Hehe.

174
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:35,880
It's about that heavy.

175
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:37,600
That's true, I suppose.

176
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,060
I don't think that at all!

177
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:43,460
Even with car navigation and airbags,
the curse makes it a huge minus!

178
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:46,620
Could this be a fateful encounter, or...

179
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:49,780
I can't think that! I can't think that!
I can't think that! I can't think that!

180
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:53,900
Well, well,
maybe the curse won't even happen anymore.

181
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,380
I don't know what circumstances there were,

182
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:04,080
as long as it drives properly,
there's no problem.

183
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,900
It's so terrifying I can't even
look in the rearview mirror.

184
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,800
It's getting dark somehow, isn't it.

185
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:22,880
Senpai.

186
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:24,760
Don't look behind you.

187
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:25,180
But...

188
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:27,000
Go slowly.

189
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:27,980
Straight ahead, okay?

190
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:30,880
I told you, senpai!

191
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:44,580
With a 100,000 yen budget,
this is about all we have here.

192
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:45,860
I'm sorry, but

193
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:49,620
maybe I just wasn't meant to have a car.

194
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:53,140
With the Honda middleman commission,
I'll make up for what I lost on the curry.

195
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:55,580
I was hoping to fill in the hole a little.

196
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:57,820
What about that one?

197
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:00,780
Senpai...

198
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,780
Nooo!

199
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,920
That's a ladder truck, isn't it!

200
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:09,600
That one's a decommissioned vehicle,
slated to be scrapped.

201
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,440
Are you gonna crush it?

202
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:14,300
Yeah, it's not fit for sale.

203
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:16,600
What a waste

204
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:20,560
For being used over ten years,
it's got low mileage too.

205
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:23,940
As for the ladder,
it's been used maybe a handful of times.

206
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,060
Hey, look!

207
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,940
It's got quite a lot of
red stuff on it, though.

208
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:39,560
I brought it. It was used by the Okumura volunteer fire brigade up in Ōgiyama until last year.
Sure, a ladder truck doesn't seem like it'd see much action out there.

209
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:41,760
Me

210
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,340
What a waste.

211
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:54,040
Isn't there some way to put this to use?

212
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:56,420
That's it!

213
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:59,540
Honda, buy this one with your 100,000 yen.

214
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:02,860
What would you even do with a fire truck?

215
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:05,200
Curry, of course! Curry!

216
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,720
What's that noise?

217
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,720
It's the car from before.

218
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:31,300
It seemed to be a ladder truck.

219
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:40,740
Alright, this spot's fine.

220
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,960
Attention, examinees, sorry to bother you.

221
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:51,560
Thank you for your hard
work studying day and night.

222
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:54,300
How's your stomach doing?

223
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:57,260
Friend of poor students, Ryotsu Curry!

224
00:13:57,260 --> 00:14:00,320
Ryotsu Curry has arrived!

225
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,520
Right, let's go.

226
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:04,380
Yes.

227
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,200
Alright, here goes!

228
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:12,860
Namaste!

229
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,840
U-um, hello.

230
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:20,700
We have large, medium, and regular portions, plus our special Passing Exam Curry.
How about that?

231
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:23,980
What exactly is that Passing Exam Curry?

232
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:27,620
It's katsu curry with a raw egg on top,
packed with nutrition.

233
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:30,360
And on top of that, you get a "Katsu-nan-chatte"
(a "you'll pass" pun).

234
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:34,020
Then one large Passing Exam Curry, please.

235
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:37,840
Coming right up, one large Passing Exam Curry!
Namaste!

236
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,540
Passing curry, large, one, Namaste!

237
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:47,260
Hello, namaste, namaste

238
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:51,160
Yes, four Passing Exam Curries,
large portions, 500 yen each.

239
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:55,060
One Passing Exam Curry over here too,
and one more over there!

240
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:56,980
Coming, coming, namaste.

241
00:14:57,580 --> 00:14:58,660
Honda-kun,

242
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:02,100
two large Passing Exam
Curries and three medium ones,

243
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:04,760
so that's two large and three medium, right?

244
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:08,720
Added on: one regular large,
and three large Passing Exam Curries.

245
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:13,100
Added on: one regular large,
and three large Passing Exam Curries.

246
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:16,400
Wait, how many large ones is that
once you add the earlier ones?

247
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:21,700
One large Passing Exam Curry was cancelled,
so a medium one came in as a replacement.

248
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:26,920
With the additions, three medium Passing Exam
Curries and one regular large have come about.

249
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,200
Three medium, plus the large ones...

250
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,860
More and more added on!

251
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:34,980
I have no idea what's what anymore,
you've made it all so confusing!

252
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:44,960
Which one is large and which one is medium?

253
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:45,460
Well, whatever.

254
00:15:45,460 --> 00:15:47,340
Honda-kun, ladder ride-on!

255
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:48,500
Namaste!

256
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:50,900
Yes, you there, large is 500 yen.

257
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,580
That one's medium, 450 yen.

258
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:54,260
Namaste!

259
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:57,940
Passing Exam Curry costs
100 yen more per liter, so

260
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,700
please have your exact change ready.

261
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:00,680
Namaste!

262
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:02,640
Namaste!

263
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,900
Namaste!

264
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,180
Namaste!

265
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,380
Namaste!

266
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:07,480
Namaste!

267
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,280
Namaste!

268
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:09,100
Namaste!

269
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:17,640
You sold out of 200 servings, didn't you.

270
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:20,580
For a first day,
wasn't that a pretty good result?

271
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:23,720
Why am I the one working at a curry shop?

272
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,560
What a brilliant tsukkomi, Honda!

273
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,860
Seriously, give me a break, senpai.

274
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:33,820
I just wanted an ordinary
car I could actually drive.

275
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,780
We went and bought a fire truck.

276
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:40,340
You were acting like a little
kid too when you saw this thing!

277
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:42,560
Even so, you didn't have to buy it.

278
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:45,040
With my hard-earned 100,000 yen,

279
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:49,460
Here's today's take.

280
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:51,540
Sorry for dragging you into this.

281
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,680
So go ahead and buy whatever car you like.

282
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,460
But you know, Honda.

283
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:58,140
A man, no matter what,

284
00:16:58,140 --> 00:17:00,640
must never forget the two words: ambition.

285
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:01,560
Ambition?

286
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:02,880
Today is good, but tomorrow is better.

287
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:04,080
And the day after tomorrow is better still.

288
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:05,580
Keep earning more and more,

289
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:08,940
ambition to become a millionaire someday,
no matter what!

290
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:16,400
My ambition is to crawl up from rock bottom
in a fire truck that's about to be scrapped.

291
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:21,180
Senpai, I'd really like to help
you at the curry shop too, please.

292
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:22,820
What, is that all right? It's fine.

293
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:28,780
But with that money, all you can buy is a
kit-car Porsche that can't even be driven outside.

294
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:33,740
If you're going to do it, then like
that rich guy, buy a Porsche with cash.

295
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:36,980
And while you're at it, I'd love to
impulse-buy a Ferrari and a Benz too.

296
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,540
That's my ambition.

297
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:43,960
Right, buy a Porsche. Buy five, six of them!

298
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,500
That's what makes a man.

299
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:48,460
We swear right here and now.

300
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:51,540
that we will fight until we've sold
all 10,000 servings of curry in stock.

301
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,680
On the name of our late grandpa.

302
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:57,140
Isn't your grandfather, senpai,
still alive in Tsukudajima?

303
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,520
On the name of our great-grandpa.

304
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:05,300
The curry's best-before
date is only six days away.

305
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,380
How are you doing, Mammoth Dutch's wife?

306
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:11,940
Taking out the garbage.

307
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:15,080
Between endless housework,

308
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:16,580
let's take it a little easy today

309
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:19,520
how about a nutritious
serving of Passing Exam Curry?

310
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:20,660
Two servings, please.

311
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:21,760
Me too, over here.

312
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:24,080
Yes, yes, coming right over!

313
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:26,860
That lady over there,
you've lost some weight, haven't you?

314
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:29,900
Look at you, and we only just met!

315
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,520
Is that so?

316
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:33,300
Says the one who talks!

317
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:35,680
Here you go, a large portion.
Make sure you have exact change.

318
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:40,360
Middle schoolers at their hungriest,
thinking of buying yakisoba bread at the kiosk

319
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,220
Namaste!

320
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:43,800
How about some piping
hot curry for a change?

321
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:48,060
Hey, what are you doing?

322
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:51,260
Namaste to all the folks in
the Marunouchi office district!

323
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:54,820
To survive this recession,
if customers won't come,

324
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:56,060
we go to them.

325
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:59,180
The passion and guts to say,
"If you won't buy, I'll make you buy!"

326
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,800
That's what matters.

327
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,920
A ladder truck What an eccentric idea.

328
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:06,660
I suppose one man's trash
is another man's treasure.

329
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:08,800
Why did you go with curry
alone as your product?

330
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,320
Because it's a game of
clearing out leftover stock.

331
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:15,100
Right? I mean,
there's hardly any unsold stock left over.

332
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:17,840
That means there's less waste, of course,

333
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:19,800
but I'm sure you've all
had this experience too.

334
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:23,240
At dinnertime, the smell of curry
drifting over from the neighborhood,

335
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:26,120
that irresistible scent that
stirs both fear and appetite.

336
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:28,640
I just thought, this is it!

337
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:31,340
I won't have to eat curry for the rest of my life,
and that's fine!

338
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:36,120
The curry shop from the ladder company,
appearing and vanishing at will,

339
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:41,100
whoever said "Namaste" to me today,

340
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:44,840
the first 100 customers get a large
curry at a huge special discount!

341
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:50,500
Okay, okay, there's still plenty of curry.

342
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:52,800
Please don't push, and line up in order.

343
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,140
Honda, what's wrong?

344
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,660
Shit, we did it.

345
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:03,540
Cheers! 10,000 servings
sold before the best-by date!

346
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,000
Ah, Honda, don't fall asleep yet!

347
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,200
There are a lot of customers waiting outside,
you know!

348
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:11,140
But we're out of curry and rice now!

349
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:12,460
Don't worry.

350
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,080
I've already arranged for more.

351
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:17,240
The curry and rice for 20,000
servings will arrive shortly.

352
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:18,520
20,000 servings.

353
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:22,120
Can't you let us rest a little, senpai?

354
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,820
I haven't slept in five days, you know.

355
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:25,060
Five days is nothing.

356
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:27,580
This is the crucial turning
point of your life, Honda!

357
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:29,800
Where did your ambitions go?

358
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,840
Ambitions.

359
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:33,320
Porsche, BMW, Ferrari.

360
00:20:33,540 --> 00:20:33,980
Benz!

361
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:36,180
Ambitions!

362
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:40,200
Yahoo!

363
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:42,100
Alright!

364
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:46,660
The new best-before date is three days from now.
Sell, sell, sell like crazy!

365
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:48,420
Namaste!

366
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:54,000
Porsche is the biggest one, Porsche is...

367
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:56,920
F-f-fire! It's a fire!

368
00:20:57,500 --> 00:21:13,260
Ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru-ru!

369
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,760
Hurry, jump over here!

370
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,260
That guy's arson trick!

371
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:21,940
What?

372
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,160
Honda!

373
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:23,820
Honda!

374
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:24,500
Yes!

375
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:29,300
Run quickly, it's a fire!

376
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,400
Honda, hurry!

377
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,040
Yes!

378
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:38,180
Damn it, I won't let them get away!

379
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:44,640
Speed up more!

380
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:48,400
We're already at full throttle, and the vehicle's too heavy.
We can't go any faster.

381
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:51,040
You're in a four-wheeler,
there's no time to get there.

382
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:53,800
That guy went and trampled on my ambitions!

383
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,340
Aren't you angry about that?

384
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:01,140
The sauce is fine.

385
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,620
Don't underestimate me.

386
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:06,360
Hey, wait!

387
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:10,080
You're really strong on two wheels

388
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:16,580
Why shoot it?
That terminal is for that purpose.

389
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:23,280
Oi, you there!

390
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:27,040
Aaaaaah!

391
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:30,280
Honda, the culprit went that way!
Bring the ladder back!

392
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:30,940
Boss!

393
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:31,440
Behind you!

394
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:35,320
I've got him!

395
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:51,280
I won't let you get away!

396
00:22:51,280 --> 00:22:55,580
Hahaha!

397
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:59,880
Aaaaaah, my curry!

398
00:23:00,220 --> 00:23:02,600
The profits from 20,000 servings!

399
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:07,400
Ryotsu, this bill is for you.

400
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:09,400
A bill?

401
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:13,540
Building damage and repair costs:
185 million yen.

402
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:18,400
Pedestrian bridge, utility poles, guardrails, and other repairs:
100 million yen.

403
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:23,380
Plus traffic violation fines and so on,
for a total of 300 million yen.

404
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:24,720
I hear they don't accept
installment payments.

405
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:26,940
That concludes today's briefing.

406
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:28,820
Wait, Chief!

407
00:23:28,820 --> 00:23:31,680
But we arrested the arsonist, didn't we?

408
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:34,040
So why am I the one who
has to pay for the damages?

409
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:35,100
Idiot!

410
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:37,680
You modified a ladder truck
and went tearing around in it!

411
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:39,320
I'm through with you.

412
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:40,860
Chief, how could you say that?

413
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:42,920
What about my Porsche?

414
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:45,620
What about my drive with Nana-chan?

415
00:23:45,620 --> 00:23:46,860
This is no time for that!

416
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:49,560
Now that the curry stock has sold out,

417
00:23:49,560 --> 00:23:50,740
we should have just quit, shouldn't we.

418
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:52,880
It's your own fault for being greedy.

419
00:23:53,380 --> 00:23:55,500
So our ambition was just a reckless dream?

420
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:59,380
Why did it come to this?

421
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:13,060
I wonder why.

422
00:24:13,060 --> 00:24:14,200
I wonder why.

423
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:14,940
I wonder why.

424
00:24:14,940 --> 00:24:16,240
I wonder why.

425
00:24:16,240 --> 00:24:18,380
Ryo-san's "I wonder why."

426
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:23,980
Ryo-san's eyebrows look like black seagulls.

427
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:24,960
I wonder why.

428
00:24:26,220 --> 00:24:30,400
He wears sandals, yet he runs super fast.

429
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:31,480
I wonder why.

430
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:38,260
Ryo-san always has his sleeves rolled up.

431
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:39,420
I wonder why.

432
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:44,600
He's a total mess,
yet everyone looks up to him.

433
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:45,740
I wonder why.

434
00:24:45,740 --> 00:24:47,980
I wonder why.

435
00:24:47,980 --> 00:24:51,640
Not that it matters,

436
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:58,380
but this anime's title is so long.

437
00:24:58,380 --> 00:25:01,160
This is Kameari Park Police Box in Katsushika Ward,
making its debut.

438
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:03,000
I wonder why.

439
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,340
I wonder why.

440
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,680
I wonder why

441
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:09,740
I wonder why

442
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:11,120
I wonder why

443
00:25:11,120 --> 00:25:11,780
I wonder why

444
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:13,980
I wonder why

445
00:25:15,980 --> 00:25:19,100
I wonder why, I wonder why,
I wonder why, I wonder why

446
00:25:30,020 --> 00:25:32,260
March 3rd is my birthday.

447
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:36,440
But on this day,
misfortune keeps raining down on me.

448
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:39,560
This year, of all years, I was determined
to get through unharmed, yet here I am.

449
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:43,220
Why the hell am I building
a life-size hina doll display?

450
00:25:43,220 --> 00:25:47,400
Next time, make sure you celebrate
my birthday properly, alright?

451
00:25:56,100 --> 00:25:56,600
Thanks.

